# Supabase — optional. Without these the app runs on the offline seed catalogue
# (src/lib/data.ts) and persists commits to localStorage only.
#
# Find both values in your Supabase project: Settings → API.
# The anon key is safe to expose to the browser; Row-Level Security (see
# supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql) guards what it can read and write.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Auth: email/password works out of the box once the vars above are set.
# For Google sign-in, enable it in Supabase → Authentication → Providers →
# Google (add a Google OAuth client id/secret), and add your app origin(s) to
# Authentication → URL Configuration → Redirect URLs.

# Payments (optional): a serverless endpoint that creates a manual-capture
# Stripe PaymentIntent and returns { paymentIntentId }. Until set, commits use a
# stubbed intent id. The capture-batch Edge Function (supabase/functions/) needs
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY + SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY set via `supabase secrets set`.
VITE_STRIPE_AUTHORIZE_URL=

# Shipping — Australia Post Parcel Post. Set these as Edge Function secrets
# (not VITE_*; they must never reach the browser) for supabase/functions/
# create-shipment:
#   AUSPOST_PAC_KEY          — Postage Assessment Calculation (rates) API key
#   AUSPOST_API_KEY          — Shipping & Tracking API key
#   AUSPOST_API_PASSWORD     — Shipping & Tracking API password (Basic auth)
#   AUSPOST_ACCOUNT_NUMBER   — your Australia Post charge account
#   AUSPOST_PRODUCT_ID       — Parcel Post product id for your account (e.g. T28)
#   AUSPOST_FROM_NAME / _LINE1 / _SUBURB / _STATE / _POSTCODE  — sender address
# Without them, create-shipment falls back to a stub article id.
